<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pura Pakualaman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">19th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Puro Pakualaman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pura Pakualaman is the palace of the Paku Alam princes in Yogyakarta, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, built in the 19th century after the founding of the house in 1813. Smaller than the sultan's kraton, it has a pendopo pavilion, a library of Javanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> and a museum, and it is still the residence of the Paku Alam, who serves as vice-governor of Yogyakarta.</p></div>
